{"causes": ["The intense nationalistic fervor during the Wars of Liberation against Napoleonic France inspired many, including women, to contribute to the Prussian war effort.", "Strict societal gender roles in early 19th-century Europe largely prohibited women from formal military service, necessitating disguise for those who wished to participate.", "The Lützow Free Corps's volunteer nature and less rigid recruitment standards compared to regular army units may have facilitated Lühring's successful enlistment under a male guise."], "effects": ["Anna Lühring's story became an early 19th-century example of female military service, challenging contemporary gender norms and sparking public discussion.", "Her actions contributed to the historical record of women's hidden participation in conflicts, inspiring later scholarship on gender and warfare.", "Lühring's recognition by Frederick William III underscored the complex societal attitudes towards female patriotism and military valor in the post-Napoleonic era."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "wars-of-liberation", "sourceName": "Wars of Liberation", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "anna-lhring", "targetName": "Anna Lühring", "context": "The patriotic fervor of the German Wars of Liberation (1813-1815) directly influenced Anna Lühring's decision to enlist in the Prussian army."}, {"sourceSlug": "anna-lhring", "sourceName": "Anna Lühring", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "napoleonic-wars", "targetName": "Napoleonic Wars", "context": "Anna Lühring actively participated as a soldier in the Prussian army during the final campaigns of the Napoleonic Wars in 1814."}, {"sourceSlug": "anna-lhring", "sourceName": "Anna Lühring", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "bremen", "targetName": "Bremen", "context": "Anna Lühring was born in Bremen in 1796, which served as her initial geographical context before her military service."}, {"sourceSlug": "lutzow-free-corps", "sourceName": "Lützow Free Corps", "verb": "CONTA